{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"find /workspace -maxdepth 3 -type f -print | sort | sed -n '1,240p'\nrg -n \\\"refund|batch|duplicate\\\" README.md packages -g '*.md' -g '*.toml' -g '*.json' -g '*.sol' | head -300\"","aggregated_output":"/workspace/DESIGN.md\n/workspace/WORKSPACE.json\n/workspace/WORKSPACE.md\n/workspace/dependency-hashes.json\n/workspace/packages/contracts/foundry.toml\n/workspace/packages/contracts/hardhat.config.ts\n/workspace/packages/contracts/package.json\n/workspace/packages/contracts/remappings.txt\n/workspace/pnpm-lock.yaml\nrg: README.md: IO error for operation on README.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:46:    // but in exchange the refund on every call to nonReentrant will be lower in\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:47:    // amount. Since refunds are capped to a percentage of the total\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:49:    // increase the likelihood of the full refund coming into effect.\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:103:        // By storing the original value once again, a refund is triggered (see\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/interfaces/draft-IERC6093.sol:157:     * Used in batch transfers.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:13:///      bearer claim until its owner atomically burns it for redemption or refund. The immutable quote token is trusted\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:32:        /// @notice Full ticket refunds are enabled and the sponsor may recover the prize NFT.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:110:    /// @notice Emitted when the raffle enters the full-refund branch.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:111:    /// @param finalizer Address that enabled refunds.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:112:    /// @param remainingRefundLiability Raw six-decimal quote-token units initially available for ticket refunds.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:147:    /// @notice Emitted when an owner burns one or more tickets for a full quote-token refund.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:148:    /// @param owner Ticket owner that burned the tickets and received the refund.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:151:    /// @param amount Raw six-decimal quote-token units refunded, equal to `entryQuantity * ENTRY_PRICE`.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:152:    /// @param remainingRefundLiability Raw six-decimal quote-token units still claimable after this refund.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:173:    /// @notice Emitted when the escrowed prize is returned after a cash result or refund transition.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:220:    /// @notice Raised when a refund batch is empty or exceeds the bounded ticket limit.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:222:    /// @param maximum Maximum ticket IDs accepted per refund transaction.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:242:    /// @notice Raised when refunds are requested before the applicable liveness deadline.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:243:    /// @param deadline Unix timestamp, in seconds, at which refunds become available.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:253:    /// @param recipient Draw requester that was due the refund.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:322:    /// @notice Enables full refunds after the sold-raffle request deadline or an accepted request's callback deadline.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:340:    /// @notice Burns an owner-selected batch of tickets and returns their full entry purchase value.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:341:    /// @dev Accepts one to 100 tickets. Duplicate, nonexistent, or foreign-owned IDs revert the entire batch.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:342:    /// @param ticketIds Ticket IDs owned by the caller and submitted for refund.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:344:    function refundTickets(uint256[] calldata ticketIds) external returns (uint256 amount);\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:384:    /// @return amount Raw six-decimal quote-token units across the unsettled pot, refunds, and allocated claims.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:410:    /// @notice Returns the prize depositor and pre-end empty-raffle refund authority.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:459:    /// @return amount Raw six-decimal quote-token units collected before settlement or refund activation.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:462:    /// @notice Returns the current aggregate full-refund liability.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffle.sol:463:    /// @return amount Raw six-decimal quote-token units still claimable by unrefunded tickets.\npackages/contracts/src/interfaces/IRaffleFactory.sol:33:    /// @param sponsor Prize depositor and pre-end empty-raffle refund authority.\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:24:///      owners burn them for redemption or refund. Each raffle is a fixed, non-upgradeable ERC-1167 clone with no\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:265:            address refundRecipient = msg.sender;\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:267:                success := call(gas(), refundRecipient, excess, 0, 0, 0, 0)\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:349:    function refundTickets(uint256[] calldata ticketIds) external override nonReentrant returns (uint256 amount) {\npackages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:505:    ///      occurs. In-flight, late, wrong-request, duplicate, and ABI-decodable wrong-length callbacks are ignored for\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
