{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/Clones.sol | sed -n '25,90p'\ncat WORKSPACE.md\ncat packages/contracts/package.json\ncat packages/contracts/foundry.toml\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/Clones.sol | sed -n '25,90p'\ncat WORKSPACE.md\ncat packages/contracts/package.json\ncat packages/contracts/foundry.toml\"","aggregated_output":"    25\t     *\n    26\t     * This function uses the create opcode, which should never revert.\n    27\t     *\n    28\t     * WARNING: This function does not check if `implementation` has code. A clone that points to an address\n    29\t     * without code cannot be initialized. Initialization calls may appear to be successful when, in reality, they\n    30\t     * have no effect and leave the clone uninitialized, allowing a third party to initialize it later.\n    31\t     */\n    32\t    function clone(address implementation) internal returns (address instance) {\n    33\t        return clone(implementation, 0);\n    34\t    }\n    35\t\n    36\t    /**\n    37\t     * @dev Same as {xref-Clones-clone-address-}[clone], but with a `value` parameter to send native currency\n    38\t     * to the new contract.\n    39\t     *\n    40\t     * WARNING: This function does not check if `implementation` has code. A clone that points to an address\n    41\t     * without code cannot be initialized. Initialization calls may appear to be successful when, in reality, they\n    42\t     * have no effect and leave the clone uninitialized, allowing a third party to initialize it later.\n    43\t     *\n    44\t     * NOTE: Using a non-zero value at creation will require the contract using this function (e.g. a factory)\n    45\t     * to always have enough balance for new deployments. Consider exposing this function under a payable method.\n    46\t     */\n    47\t    function clone(address implementation, uint256 value) internal returns (address instance) {\n    48\t        if (address(this).balance < value) {\n    49\t            revert Errors.InsufficientBalance(address(this).balance, value);\n    50\t        }\n    51\t        assembly (\"memory-safe\") {\n    52\t            // Cleans the upper 96 bits of the `implementation` word, then packs the first 3 bytes\n    53\t            // of the `implementation` address with the bytecode before the address.\n    54\t            mstore(0x00, or(shr(232, shl(96, implementation)), 0x3d602d80600a3d3981f3363d3d373d3d3d363d73000000))\n    55\t            // Packs the remaining 17 bytes of `implementation` with the bytecode after the address.\n    56\t            mstore(0x20, or(shl(120, implementation), 0x5af43d82803e903d91602b57fd5bf3))\n    57\t            instance := create(value, 0x09, 0x37)\n    58\t        }\n    59\t        if (instance == address(0)) {\n    60\t            revert Errors.FailedDeployment();\n    61\t        }\n    62\t    }\n    63\t\n    64\t    /**\n    65\t     * @dev Deploys and returns the address of a clone that mimics the behavior of `implementation`.\n    66\t     *\n    67\t     * This function uses the create2 opcode and a `salt` to deterministically deploy\n    68\t     * the clone. Using the same `implementation` and `salt` multiple times will revert, since\n    69\t     * the clones cannot be deployed twice at the same address.\n    70\t     *\n    71\t     * WARNING: This function does not check if `implementation` has code. A clone that points to an address\n    72\t     * without code cannot be initialized. Initialization calls may appear to be successful when, in reality, they\n    73\t     * have no effect and leave the clone uninitialized, allowing a third party to initialize it later.\n    74\t     */\n    75\t    function cloneDeterministic(address implementation, bytes32 salt) internal returns (address instance) {\n    76\t        return cloneDeterministic(implementation, salt, 0);\n    77\t    }\n    78\t\n    79\t    /**\n    80\t     * @dev Same as {xref-Clones-cloneDeterministic-address-bytes32-}[cloneDeterministic], but with\n    81\t     * a `value` parameter to send native currency to the new contract.\n    82\t     *\n    83\t     * WARNING: This function does not check if `implementation` has code. A clone that points to an address\n    84\t     * without code cannot be initialized. Initialization calls may appear to be successful when, in reality, they\n    85\t     * have no effect and leave the clone uninitialized, allowing a third party to initialize it later.\n    86\t     *\n    87\t     * NOTE: Using a non-zero value at creation will require the contract using this function (e.g. a factory)\n    88\t     * to always have enough balance for new deployments. Consider exposing this function under a payable method.\n    89\t     */\n    90\t    function cloneDeterministic(\n# Dependency Workspace\n\nCurrent working directory / primary repository root: /workspace\nWorkspace manifest: WORKSPACE.json\nDependency repositories are checked out as top-level directories inside the same workspace root.\nWhen reporting file_path for dependency code, prefix it with the dependency alias directory.\nPrimary repository: clean-context @ LOCAL_SNAPSHOT\nNo dependency checkouts are listed in WORKSPACE.json.\n\nPath guidance:\n- Reference primary repo files relative to the workspace root.\n- Reference dependency files with their dependency directory prefix, e.g. `agave/...`.\n{\n  \"name\": \"@raffle-fun/contracts\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=22.13 <23\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"hardhat compile && forge build\",\n    \"compile\": \"hardhat compile\",\n    \"test\": \"pnpm test:foundry && pnpm test:hardhat\",\n    \"test:foundry\": \"forge test\",\n    \"test:hardhat\": \"hardhat test nodejs\",\n    \"coverage\": \"forge coverage --report lcov --no-match-coverage '^(script/|src/mocks/|test/)' && node scripts/check-coverage.mjs\",\n    \"gas\": \"forge snapshot --check -j 1 --no-match-test '^(testFuzz|invariant)'\",\n    \"gas:update\": \"forge snapshot -j 1 --no-match-test '^(testFuzz|invariant)'\",\n    \"fmt\": \"forge fmt\",\n    \"fmt:check\": \"forge fmt --check\",\n    \"lint\": \"solhint 'src/**/*.sol' 'test/**/*.sol'\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"slither\": \"slither . --config-file slither.config.json\",\n    \"deploy:sepolia\": \"hardhat ignition deploy ignition/modules/RaffleFun.ts --network sepolia\",\n    \"verify:sepolia\": \"hardhat ignition verify chain-11155111\",\n    \"deployment:write\": \"tsx scripts/write-deployment.ts\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@chainlink/contracts\": \"1.5.0\",\n    \"@openzeppelin/contracts\": \"5.6.1\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@nomicfoundation/hardhat-ignition\": \"3.1.8\",\n    \"@nomicfoundation/hardhat-ignition-viem\": \"3.1.6\",\n    \"@nomicfoundation/hardhat-toolbox-viem\": \"5.0.7\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"26.1.2\",\n    \"dotenv\": \"17.4.2\",\n    \"hardhat\": \"3.11.1\",\n    \"solhint\": \"6.2.3\",\n    \"tsx\": \"4.23.1\",\n    \"typescript\": \"6.0.3\",\n    \"viem\": \"2.55.10\",\n    \"zod\": \"4.4.3\"\n  }\n}\n[profile.default]\nsrc = \"src\"\ntest = \"test/foundry\"\nscript = \"script\"\nout = \"out\"\nlibs = [\"lib\", \"node_modules\"]\nsolc_version = \"0.8.36\"\nevm_version = \"cancun\"\noptimizer = true\noptimizer_runs = 200\nvia_ir = false\nfuzz = { runs = 1_000, seed = \"0x524146464c45\" }\ninvariant = { runs = 256, depth = 64, fail_on_revert = false }\ngas_reports = [\"Raffle\", \"RaffleFactory\"]\n\n[profile.ci]\nfuzz = { runs = 10_000 }\ninvariant = { runs = 1_000, depth = 256, fail_on_revert = false }\n\n[profile.audit]\nfuzz = { runs = 100_000, seed = \"0x41554449545f46555a5a\" }\ninvariant = { runs = 1_000, depth = 256, fail_on_revert = false }\n\n[profile.audit_strict]\nfuzz = { runs = 10_000, seed = \"0x41554449545f535452494354\" }\ninvariant = { runs = 1_000, depth = 256, fail_on_revert = true }\n\n[profile.audit_release]\nfuzz = { runs = 100_000, seed = \"0x52454c454153455f43414d504149474e\" }\ninvariant = { runs = 5_000, depth = 512, fail_on_revert = true, timeout = 3_600 }\n\n[profile.coverage]\nvia_ir = false\noptimizer = false\n\n[profile.comparison]\nvia_ir = true\noptimizer = true\noptimizer_runs = 1_000\n\n[fmt]\nline_length = 120\ntab_width = 4\nbracket_spacing = true\nint_types = \"long\"\nquote_style = \"double\"\nnumber_underscore = \"thousands\"\nsort_imports = true\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
